# `todo/t1077` REGRESSION CELL — payload: `String`, storage class: `.rodata`
# LITERAL, consume shape: WHOLE-VALUE ASSIGN into a `String` local.
#
# The third face of one payload at one storage class. Print it directly and
# both lanes are silently wrong (`box_nested_deref_rodata_string_print.gg`);
# assign it to a local and the COMPILER panics instead:
#
#   PRE-fix, BOTH lanes: build rc 101
#     Tier 2a consume-site violation: 1 violation(s) ...
#     fn @main bb0 i10 — AssignIntoOwnedSlot(dst: GorgetString) — untracked
#     source consumed (ownership not decided)
#
# ⚠ BOTH LANES, IDENTICALLY — the panic is at GIR level, before either backend
# runs, so there is no lane asymmetry in this cell. That is one more piece of
# evidence for the single-root-cause claim: every face in this class comes from
# the same wrong GIR, and the lanes differ only in what they do downstream of
# it.
#
# EXPECTED OUTPUT: hi
# EXPECTED EXIT: 0 on BOTH backends.
#
# ⛔ `known_gaps/` with a LIVE test: self-host cannot compile nested `Box`
# (`todo/t1311`) AND this leaks at scope exit (`todo/t1309`).

void main():
    Box[Box[String]] w = Box.new(Box.new("hi"))
    String s = (*(*w))
    print(s)
